# RUNBOOK — bix-43-q1 enrichment completion (one click on a connected runner)

All DE artifacts are already produced (do NOT re-run DE unless desired; script is deterministic).

## A. Connected runner (has internet)
1. `pip install gseapy`            # needs PyPI egress
2. `python analysis/run_enrichment_connected.py`   # from /workspace; reads results/*.csv, needs no DE recompute
3. Read `results/enrichment_branches/summary.json`:
   - `prerank_main`: keys `term` (GO BP full name), `FDR q-val`, `NES` (sign = up/down in combination), `p-value`. This is the MAIN branch (no threshold dependence).
   - `a_ttest_padj05`, `b_top150_combined/up/down`, `b_top300_combined/up/down`: each has `term`, `Adjusted P-value`, `Overlap`, `Genes`.
   - Per-branch top-20 tables: `results/enrichment_branches/ora_*_top20.csv`, `prerank_main_top20.csv`.
4. Final answer field (question asks for "lowest adjusted p-value"): quote the ORA branch
   `Adjusted P-value` (Enrichr server-side BH; background = Enrichr default library background).
   Priority per researcher: (a) `a_ttest_padj05`; then top-N branches. Report `prerank_main` FDR term in parallel;
   if branches disagree, list all minima and name the most robust (appearing in both branches / same parent pathway).

## B. Connected runner without gseapy install, or offline runner with a provided GMT
1. Download Enrichr library once (any connected machine):
   `curl -L "https://maayanlab.cloud/Enrichr/geneSetLibrary?mode=text&libraryName=GO_Biological_Process_2021" -o go_bp_2021.gmt`
2a. With gseapy: `gseapy.enrich(gene_list=..., gene_sets="go_bp_2021.gmt")` / `gseapy.prerank(gene_sets="go_bp_2021.gmt")`
    (or pass a dict parsed from the GMT). NOTE: local `gseapy.enrich` uses hypergeometric + own BH (background = input universe); values may differ from Enrichr server.
2b. Without gseapy (explicit deviation from the gseapy+Enrichr requirement — must be flagged in the answer):
   `python analysis/local_enrich_fallback.py --gmt go_bp_2021.gmt \
      --rnk results/rnk_all_genes_combination9_vs_DMSO3.csv \
      --genes results/de_alt_ttest_log2cpm.csv --universe results/de_full_combination9_vs_DMSO3.csv \
      --out results/enrichment_local`
   Read `results/enrichment_local/local_ora_top20.csv` (lowest "Adjusted P-value") and
   `local_prerank_top20.csv` (lowest "FDR q-val").

